  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want a separate network for each of our 48 hepatocellular carcinoma patients showing how both TFs and miRNAs regulate genes. I have the gene-by-sample expression matrix, a motif prior, a PPI file and a miRNA target list with one miRNA ID per line. I'm not sure whether my committee will want a figure for every patient."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Did you mean LIONESS-PUMA's result? LIONESS-PUMA's contract: \"Infer aggregate PUMA and sample-specific LIONESS-PUMA networks\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: I want a separate network for each of our 48 hepatocellular carcinoma patients showing how both TFs and miRNAs regulate genes. I have the gene-by-sample expression matrix, a motif prior, a PPI file and a miRNA target list with one miRNA ID per line. I'm not sure whether my committee will want a figure for every patient.\nUser follow-up: I'm looking for per-patient networks with both TF and miRNA regulators."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want a separate network for each of our 48 hepatocellular carcinoma patients showing how both TFs and miRNAs regulate genes.\" -- available from LIONESS-PUMA.\n2. \"I'm looking for per-patient networks with both TF and miRNA regulators.\" -- available from LIONESS-PUMA.\n\nFor the sample-specific output you described, use **LIONESS-PUMA**.\n\nRequired inputs:\n   - `expression_file`: Expression matrix\n   - `motif_file`: Motif/prior\n   - `ppi_file`: PPI network\n   - `mirna_file`: miRNA list\n\nOutputs:\n   - Aggregate network (`output_file`).\n   - Sample-specific network for each patient/sample (`lioness_output`).\n\nYou do not need to run **PUMA** separately; **LIONESS-PUMA** also produces the aggregate output. Use **PUMA** alone only when a cohort-level aggregate result is sufficient.\n\nCost: LIONESS runs PUMA once on all samples and once more without each sample, so N samples take N+1 PUMA runs and give N network files (for your 48 patients, 49 PUMA runs). Plan the runtime and disk space, and filter edges before downstream statistics.\n\nOut-degree measures how strongly a TF is wired to its targets in each sample. If you mean TF activity instead -- how active a TF is apart from its own mRNA level -- GIRAFFE's TF-by-sample activity matrix is the other reading, from the expression, motif and PPI inputs.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
